  "tokens": [
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The three structures `std::algebra` names, at the domain that has all of" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// them." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Written intervals are a group: they compose, they have a unit, and every one" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// of them has an inverse (Open Music Theory, `016-intervals.md`, whose generic" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// and specific naming is what the two coordinates record). That group acts on" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// written pitches and on spelled pitch classes, which is what `up` and `down`" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// have always meant. And on pitches alone the action is *simply transitive* —" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// exactly one interval carries any pitch to any other — which is what makes" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// pitch and interval a torsor and what `difference` below asks." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The distinction the file exists to show is between the two carriers. A pitch" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// and a pitch differ by one interval; a spelled pitch class and a spelled pitch" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// class differ by infinitely many, because `P8` moves every class to itself" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// (Open Music Theory, `005-half-steps-whole-steps-and-accidentals.md`, for the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// spelling both carriers keep). So `Torsor` is at `Pitch` and not at" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// `NoteName`, and the missing instance is a fact about the quotient rather than" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// an omission." },
    { "kind": "piece", "text": "piece" },
    { "kind": "string", "text": "\"Pitch Algebra\"" },
